Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:47:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Accept the fno:Parameter of GREL parameters
 (grel:valueParam)

The built-in GREL functions are declared with the fno:predicate of their
parameters (grel:valueParameter, grel:param_int_i_from...). A parameter map
names the fno:Parameter itself in the RML-FNML test cases of the W3C
KG-Construct CG (rml:parameter grel:valueParam), so the function got no
argument: "to_upper_case() missing 1 required positional argument" in
RMLFNMLTC0002, 0004, 0005, 0007, 0008, 0021, 0041, 0051, 0071 and 0081.

The fno:Parameters of grel.ttl are now accepted as synonyms of their
predicates (GREL_PARAMETER_PREDICATES); the declared IRI keeps precedence.
Test: test/fno-parameters (RMLFNMLTC0002-CSV).
